    "definition": [
      {
        "key": "section:1. Business overview",
        "value": "Atlys is a digital visa platform. Travellers discover visa requirements for a\ndestination, start an application, upload their passport, and pay. The product's\nnorth-star is **conversion**: turning a v",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "section:7. How to analyse the funnel",
        "value": "- Compute step counts as `uniq(user_id)` (or `application_id` past application start)\n  per stage, in `timestamp` order, over a time window. Prefer\n  `windowFunnel`/`sequenceMatch` over per-table row ",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "section:Atlys Analytics \u2014 Base Context Layer",
        "value": "> This is the shared business + data context for the analytics agents. It describes\n> what Atlys does, the conversion funnel we optimise, the events we capture, the\n> metrics we track, and the quirks ",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      }
    ],
    "entity": [
      {
        "key": "Application",
        "value": "one visa application, identified by `application_id`. Created at the **application_started** step, so events *before* it (card clicks, searches) carry an empty `application_id`. The application record",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "Destination",
        "value": "the target country, ISO-2 code in `destination`. Each destination belongs to a region (GCC, SEA, Schengen, Americas, \u2026) with its own visa types.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "Document",
        "value": "the passport captured during KYC, recorded in `document_uploaded`. The client records the capture mode, the number of retries (`retry_count`), and whether the user crossed the failed-capture threshold",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "Event",
        "value": "one row in one of the eight raw event tables. Every event shares the common envelope (device, os, geo, app version, session, timestamps) plus event-specific columns. Events are the grain of all analys",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "User",
        "value": "a traveller. Identified by `user_id` (a 28-char string), present on every event. A user may browse many destinations and start multiple applications.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "section:2. Entity definitions",
        "value": "---",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "section:6. Entity relationships (join map)",
        "value": "- `destination_card_clicked.user_id` \u2192 all tables (`user_id`)\n- `application_started.application_id` \u2192 `document_uploaded`, `pay_now_clicked`,\n  `purchase_completed` (on `application_id`)\n- supporting",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "segment cuts",
        "value": "`device_type` / `os`, `geoip_country_code`, `destination`, `citizenship`, `co_travelers`, acquisition (`gclid` present \u21d2 paid search)",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      }
    ],
    "known_issue": [
      {
        "key": "K1",
        "value": "iOS WebKit OTP autofill regression.** On recent iOS builds the payment OTP field fails to autofill, and some users abandon at the pay step. Payment-heavy geos (Gulf card users) are most exposed. Watch",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "K2",
        "value": "Passport scan model update (Apr 2026).** The on-device passport model was updated in early April. Some Android devices report more capture failures since; being monitored.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "K3",
        "value": "MRZ OCR weaker on non-Latin passports.** Passports with non-Latin machine-readable zones need more capture retries.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "K4",
        "value": "Schengen summer slot scarcity (Apr\u2013Jun).** Appointment slots for Schengen destinations are scarce in summer; expect seasonal softness, not a bug.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "K5",
        "value": "WhatsApp nudge launch (Feb 2026).** A WhatsApp re-engagement nudge went live in February; it can lift returns to the funnel for previously-dropped users.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "K6",
        "value": "SUMMER20 coupon campaign.** A `SUMMER20` promo ran in Q2; expect elevated `coupon_applied` and lower realised `value`.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "K7",
        "value": "App 7.45 rollout.** App version 7.45.x rolled out mid-quarter; minor funnel-timing shifts around the rollout are expected.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "section:5. Known-issues log",
        "value": "---",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      }
    ],
    "metric": [
      {
        "key": "Conversion rate",
        "value": "completed purchases \u00f7 **sessions**. A session is a single app-open / web visit. This is the headline number reported to leadership.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "Drop-off rate (per funnel stage)",
        "value": "1 \u2212 (users at stage N+1 \u00f7 users at stage N), counting distinct `user_id` reaching each stage in order within the window.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "On-time delivery rate",
        "value": "applications issued on or before `visa_issuance_eta_days` \u00f7 applications issued. (Reported by the fulfilment team from post-purchase systems; not computable from the funnel tables here.)",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "Passport-capture pass rate",
        "value": "document uploads that did **not** cross the failed-capture threshold (`is_crossed_failed_attempt_threshold = 0`) \u00f7 document uploads.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "Revenue per conversion",
        "value": "`value` on `purchase_completed`, in the event's `currency`.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "Step-through rate",
        "value": "users at stage N+1 \u00f7 users at stage N.",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "section:4. Metric definitions",
        "value": "> Note on funnel conversion: within the funnel, we treat **conversion as\n> `purchase_completed` users \u00f7 users who started an application**\n> (`application_started`). This is the denominator used in th",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      }
    ],
    "relationship": [
      {
        "key": "shared app_session_id",
        "value": "application_started.app_session_id = auth_completed.app_session_id = destination_card_clicked.app_session_id = document_uploaded.app_session_id = landing_page_scrolled.app_session_id = pay_now_clicked",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "shared application_id",
        "value": "application_started.application_id = auth_completed.application_id = destination_card_clicked.application_id = document_uploaded.application_id = landing_page_scrolled.application_id = pay_now_clicked",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "shared user_id",
        "value": "application_started.user_id = auth_completed.user_id = destination_card_clicked.user_id = document_uploaded.user_id = landing_page_scrolled.user_id = pay_now_clicked.user_id = purchase_completed.user_",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      }
    ],
    "table": [
      {
        "key": "application_started",
        "value": "funnel \u2014 user starts an application \u2014 `purpose`, `eta_shown`, `co_travelers`, `destination`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "application_started",
        "value": "33 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "auth_completed",
        "value": "supporting \u2014 user finishes login/signup \u2014 `auth_method`, `is_new_user`, `attempts`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "auth_completed",
        "value": "33 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "destination_card_clicked",
        "value": "funnel \u2014 user taps a destination card \u2014 `destination`, `visa_type`, `card_type`, `flow`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "destination_card_clicked",
        "value": "35 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "document_uploaded",
        "value": "funnel \u2014 passport image submitted \u2014 `doc_type`, `capture_mode`, `retry_count`, `is_crossed_failed_attempt_threshold`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "document_uploaded",
        "value": "36 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "landing_page_scrolled",
        "value": "supporting \u2014 user scrolls a landing page \u2014 `scroll_depth_pct`, `time_on_page_s`, `page_version`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "landing_page_scrolled",
        "value": "33 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "pay_now_clicked",
        "value": "supporting \u2014 user taps Pay Now at checkout \u2014 `payment_method`, `amount`, `currency`, `coupon_applied`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "pay_now_clicked",
        "value": "35 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "purchase_completed",
        "value": "funnel \u2014 payment succeeds (**conversion**) \u2014 `value` (revenue), `currency`, `insurance_amount`, `coupon_applied`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "purchase_completed",
        "value": "38 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "search_typed",
        "value": "supporting \u2014 user types a destination search \u2014 `search_term`, `results_count`, `source`",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      },
      {
        "key": "search_typed",
        "value": "33 columns",
        "source": "clickhouse"
      },
      {
        "key": "section:3. The eight raw event tables",
        "value": "All eight are raw event streams (one table per event), joined on `user_id` and\n`application_id`, ordered in time by `timestamp`. Four are the **conversion funnel**;\nfour are **supporting** engagement ",
        "source": "base_context.md"
      }
    ]
  },
  "issues": [
    {
      "kind": "contradiction",
      "severity": "high",
      "subject": "relationship:shared application_id",
      "detail": "The relationship states that pre-application events like `destination_card_clicked` share an `application_id`, but the Application entity definition explicitly states that application_id is created at the `application_started` step and that events *before* it carry an empty `application_id`."
    },
    {
      "kind": "gap",
      "severity": "high",
      "subject": "metric:Revenue per conversion",
      "detail": "metric is named but has no executable formula or denominator"
